            <ArticleTitle>New strategies for cancer immunotherapy: targeting regulatory T cells.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1186/s13073-017-0402-8</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The immunosuppressive action of regulatory T (Treg) cells is one mechanism attributed to the limited success of cancer immunotherapies with checkpoint blockers. Two recent studies report distinct transcriptional profiles of tumor-infiltrating Treg cells and expression of specific molecules, suggesting novel strategies to overcome resistance to cancer immunotherapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
